1
00:01:33,030 --> 00:01:35,020
[Forging Justice]

2
00:01:35,229 --> 00:01:37,840
[Episode 10]

3
00:01:39,920 --> 00:01:41,509
The convicted, Qiao Zhiliang,

4
00:01:41,509 --> 00:01:43,200
raped the victim to death.

5
00:01:44,240 --> 00:01:45,840
The defendant, Li Xiang, ignored the facts

6
00:01:45,840 --> 00:01:47,229
and pleaded not guilty for him.

7
00:01:47,229 --> 00:01:49,000
If this isn't shielding a criminal,
what is?

8
00:01:49,000 --> 00:01:50,509
The defendant is Qiao Zhiliang's

9
00:01:50,509 --> 00:01:51,440
defense lawyer.

10
00:01:51,640 --> 00:01:53,350
Through reviewing the evidence,

11
00:01:53,350 --> 00:01:54,009
he believed

12
00:01:54,310 --> 00:01:55,310
that Qiao Zhiliang's actions

13
00:01:55,310 --> 00:01:56,840
did not constitute a crime.

14
00:01:59,710 --> 00:02:00,560
Then what kind of defense

15
00:02:00,560 --> 00:02:01,640
should he make

16
00:02:02,200 --> 00:02:03,640
for his client?

17
00:02:06,840 --> 00:02:08,840
Should he side with the prosecutor?

18
00:02:11,910 --> 00:02:12,710
If so,

19
00:02:13,840 --> 00:02:15,080
what is the point

20
00:02:15,430 --> 00:02:16,290
of his defense?

21
00:02:17,870 --> 00:02:20,150
Before the court formally heard the case,

22
00:02:20,150 --> 00:02:20,950
the defendant

23
00:02:21,000 --> 00:02:21,940
had already revealed to the convicted,
Qiao Zhiliang,

24
00:02:21,940 --> 00:02:23,280
the inside information regarding

25
00:02:23,280 --> 00:02:25,150
the prosecution's potential

26
00:02:25,360 --> 00:02:27,079
death penalty recommendation.

27
00:02:27,079 --> 00:02:29,000
This constitutes a leak of state secrets.

28
00:02:29,000 --> 00:02:30,060
When the defendant

29
00:02:30,079 --> 00:02:31,590
met with Qiao Zhiliang,

30
00:02:32,310 --> 00:02:33,630
he told him about the possible

31
00:02:33,630 --> 00:02:35,490
sentencing result he might face.

32
00:02:36,430 --> 00:02:37,160
Please note,

33
00:02:38,520 --> 00:02:39,850
it's a possible result.

34
00:02:40,829 --> 00:02:42,530
The purpose was to persuade Qiao Zhiliang

35
00:02:42,530 --> 00:02:44,060
to cooperate with the trial

36
00:02:44,560 --> 00:02:46,290
and fight for his legal rights.

37
00:02:46,710 --> 00:02:48,040
What's wrong with that?

38
00:02:48,520 --> 00:02:49,190
If

39
00:02:49,700 --> 00:02:51,520
their meeting and discussion of the case

40
00:02:51,520 --> 00:02:52,720
constitutes a crime,

41
00:02:53,150 --> 00:02:55,280
how can lawyers fulfill their duties?

42
00:02:59,170 --> 00:03:00,830
In our evidence Exhibit No. 4,

43
00:03:00,960 --> 00:03:02,160
when the prosecution

44
00:03:02,240 --> 00:03:03,710
interrogated Qiao Zhiliang,

45
00:03:03,710 --> 00:03:05,770
they also analyzed the case with him.

46
00:03:05,910 --> 00:03:06,870
They mentioned that

47
00:03:06,870 --> 00:03:07,960
if his attitude was bad,

48
00:03:07,960 --> 00:03:09,580
he might face the death penalty.

49
00:03:09,580 --> 00:03:11,240
After Qiao Zhiliang was detained,

50
00:03:11,240 --> 00:03:13,000
the first to meet him were
the public security authorities,

51
00:03:13,000 --> 00:03:14,030
then the prosecution,

52
00:03:14,030 --> 00:03:15,830
and finally the defense lawyer.

53
00:03:16,190 --> 00:03:17,470
Does this mean

54
00:03:18,190 --> 00:03:20,000
that the first to leak the information

55
00:03:20,000 --> 00:03:21,200
was the prosecution?

56
00:03:25,960 --> 00:03:28,740
When the prosecution discusses the case,
it's performing official duties.

57
00:03:28,740 --> 00:03:31,470
When the defense lawyer does the same,
it's leaking secrets.

58
00:03:31,470 --> 00:03:33,270
What's the legal basis for that?

59
00:03:37,560 --> 00:03:38,220
In summary,

60
00:03:38,680 --> 00:03:39,680
the prosecutor submits

61
00:03:39,680 --> 00:03:41,840
that the defendant's actions
constitute a crime

62
00:03:41,840 --> 00:03:44,520
and should be severely punished
according to the law.

63
00:03:44,520 --> 00:03:45,340
We await

64
00:03:45,370 --> 00:03:46,700
making a fair judgment.

65
00:03:48,470 --> 00:03:49,079
Defender.

66
00:04:02,680 --> 00:04:04,280
Respected Presiding Judge,

67
00:04:04,560 --> 00:04:05,620
Associate Judges,

68
00:04:06,480 --> 00:04:07,880
and People's Assessors.

69
00:04:08,430 --> 00:04:09,030
May I ask,

70
00:04:10,000 --> 00:04:10,750
in the court,

71
00:04:12,190 --> 00:04:12,910
even if

72
00:04:13,430 --> 00:04:14,230
the defendant

73
00:04:15,030 --> 00:04:17,120
is a heinous criminal,

74
00:04:18,310 --> 00:04:19,240
does he not still

75
00:04:19,310 --> 00:04:20,630
have lawful rights?

76
00:04:23,600 --> 00:04:24,730
Should those rights

77
00:04:25,190 --> 00:04:26,870
be protected or not?

78
00:04:29,560 --> 00:04:30,120
Just now,

79
00:04:30,600 --> 00:04:31,600
regarding the evidence

80
00:04:31,600 --> 00:04:33,040
presented by the prosecution,

81
00:04:33,040 --> 00:04:34,240
we have no objection.

82
00:04:34,750 --> 00:04:35,360
Moreover,

83
00:04:36,000 --> 00:04:37,510
we have also included it
in our own evidence.

84
00:04:37,510 --> 00:04:38,159
Why?

85
00:04:38,640 --> 00:04:39,909
Because this evidence

86
00:04:41,070 --> 00:04:42,370
not only proves

87
00:04:43,600 --> 00:04:45,400
that the defendant is innocent,

88
00:04:45,630 --> 00:04:46,510
but also proves

89
00:04:47,390 --> 00:04:48,240
that he,

90
00:04:48,390 --> 00:04:49,390
as a lawyer,

91
00:04:50,120 --> 00:04:51,120
faithfully

92
00:04:51,610 --> 00:04:52,970
fulfilled his

93
00:04:52,990 --> 00:04:54,050
statutory duties.

94
00:04:54,270 --> 00:04:55,159
In court,

95
00:04:55,510 --> 00:04:56,950
he fought for his client's

96
00:04:56,950 --> 00:04:59,240
legal rights to the best of his ability.

97
00:05:00,670 --> 00:05:02,040
We don't think

98
00:05:02,070 --> 00:05:02,680
that makes him

99
00:05:02,680 --> 00:05:04,310
an exceptionally outstanding lawyer.

100
00:05:04,310 --> 00:05:05,240
On the contrary,

101
00:05:05,800 --> 00:05:06,630
we believe

102
00:05:07,800 --> 00:05:09,240
he simply fulfilled

103
00:05:09,750 --> 00:05:11,800
the most basic statutory duties

104
00:05:12,190 --> 00:05:13,020
of a lawyer.

105
00:05:13,390 --> 00:05:14,520
If he hadn't done so,

106
00:05:14,560 --> 00:05:16,760
he would have been derelict in his duty.

107
00:05:18,810 --> 00:05:19,780
A defense lawyer

108
00:05:19,870 --> 00:05:22,070
has only two options:

109
00:05:22,360 --> 00:05:23,890
plead guilty with leniency

110
00:05:23,920 --> 00:05:25,050
or plead not guilty.

111
00:05:25,360 --> 00:05:26,410
If the latter

112
00:05:26,430 --> 00:05:28,290
equates to shielding a criminal,

113
00:05:29,480 --> 00:05:30,390
then the defendant

114
00:05:30,390 --> 00:05:31,360
has only one fate:

115
00:05:31,360 --> 00:05:32,190
confess and accept punishment,

116
00:05:32,190 --> 00:05:34,250
even if they are wrongfully accused.

117
00:05:40,390 --> 00:05:42,600
Are there no wrongful convictions
in this world?

118
00:05:42,600 --> 00:05:43,560
Have public prosecutors never

119
00:05:43,560 --> 00:05:44,420
made mistakes?

120
00:05:46,730 --> 00:05:48,310
The existence of the lawyer system

121
00:05:48,310 --> 00:05:50,310
is to prevent wrongful convictions

122
00:05:50,720 --> 00:05:52,580
to the greatest extent possible.

123
00:06:02,310 --> 00:06:03,190
If one day

124
00:06:03,830 --> 00:06:05,750
one of you unfortunately
becomes a defendant,

125
00:06:05,750 --> 00:06:06,390
what then?

126
00:06:09,310 --> 00:06:10,310
Without

127
00:06:10,430 --> 00:06:11,360
a reasonable

128
00:06:11,750 --> 00:06:13,000
institutional design

129
00:06:13,000 --> 00:06:13,870
to protect

130
00:06:14,030 --> 00:06:15,560
your most basic legal rights—

131
00:06:15,560 --> 00:06:17,090
how could you seek justice?

132
00:06:20,870 --> 00:06:21,870
Any one of us

133
00:06:23,830 --> 00:06:25,290
is powerless and helpless

134
00:06:26,120 --> 00:06:27,000
in the face

135
00:06:28,480 --> 00:06:29,810
of the state machinery.

136
00:06:33,600 --> 00:06:34,460
Lawyer Li Xiang

137
00:06:35,120 --> 00:06:36,480
became a defendant

138
00:06:36,560 --> 00:06:37,980
for defending someone else.

139
00:06:37,980 --> 00:06:39,510
By the prosecutor's logic,

140
00:06:39,870 --> 00:06:41,730
then I should also be a defendant.

141
00:06:42,360 --> 00:06:43,040
Likewise,

142
00:06:43,560 --> 00:06:44,690
if someone stands up

143
00:06:45,040 --> 00:06:46,480
the biggest threat to the legal system?

144
00:06:46,480 --> 00:06:48,140
they'd be a defendant as well.

145
00:06:49,630 --> 00:06:50,960
Isn't that terrifying?

146
00:06:51,950 --> 00:06:53,010
Isn't that absurd?

147
00:06:55,270 --> 00:06:56,670
Isn't this chain of logic

148
00:06:58,510 --> 00:06:59,640
the greatest threat

149
00:06:59,800 --> 00:07:01,870
to the rule of law?

150
00:07:05,190 --> 00:07:06,120
We are here today

151
00:07:06,680 --> 00:07:07,880
not just for Li Xiang,

152
00:07:08,160 --> 00:07:09,720
not just for the lawyer system.

153
00:07:09,720 --> 00:07:10,390
We are here

154
00:07:10,680 --> 00:07:11,830
to defend

155
00:07:12,070 --> 00:07:13,330
every single one of us.

156
00:07:13,800 --> 00:07:14,660
I can't promise

157
00:07:14,800 --> 00:07:15,560
we'll win.

158
00:07:16,040 --> 00:07:17,100
But I believe this—

159
00:07:17,720 --> 00:07:19,190
if I end up

160
00:07:20,120 --> 00:07:21,510
in that dock

161
00:07:22,510 --> 00:07:24,160
for defending someone today,

162
00:07:24,160 --> 00:07:25,950
somebody will definitely stand up

163
00:07:25,950 --> 00:07:27,240
to plead not guilty for me.

164
00:07:27,240 --> 00:07:28,040
If he, in turn,

165
00:07:28,240 --> 00:07:29,450
ends up in that dock

166
00:07:29,480 --> 00:07:30,750
for defending me,

167
00:07:30,870 --> 00:07:31,470
likewise,

168
00:07:31,510 --> 00:07:33,040
someone else will stand up.

169
00:07:33,120 --> 00:07:33,980
They will rise!

170
00:07:34,390 --> 00:07:35,510
This relay

171
00:07:35,680 --> 00:07:37,000
will never stop.

172
00:07:39,159 --> 00:07:40,240
It will carry on.

173
00:07:47,159 --> 00:07:47,720
But

174
00:07:50,220 --> 00:07:51,130
one day

175
00:07:52,390 --> 00:07:53,480
it will stop,

176
00:07:54,510 --> 00:07:55,480
because by then,

177
00:07:56,390 --> 00:07:57,040
China

178
00:07:57,800 --> 00:08:00,460
will have embarked on the path
of the rule of law.

179
00:08:01,240 --> 00:08:02,720
Everyone's most basic

180
00:08:02,750 --> 00:08:03,750
legal rights

181
00:08:03,950 --> 00:08:05,610
will receive due protection,

182
00:08:06,040 --> 00:08:08,240
even stronger protection!

183
00:08:11,830 --> 00:08:12,630
Order! Order!

184
00:08:12,770 --> 00:08:13,860
Order in the court!

185
00:08:33,909 --> 00:08:35,270
So,

186
00:08:37,000 --> 00:08:38,299
we are very confident

187
00:08:38,460 --> 00:08:39,390
in the acquittal

188
00:08:39,510 --> 00:08:40,570
of Lawyer Li Xiang.

189
00:08:44,870 --> 00:08:45,530
That's all.

190
00:08:45,790 --> 00:08:46,510
I'm done.

191
00:08:56,510 --> 00:08:57,310
I've decided.

192
00:08:58,080 --> 00:08:59,210
I want to be a lawyer.

193
00:09:00,550 --> 00:09:02,280
You've made up your mind again?

194
00:09:02,390 --> 00:09:03,520
I've decided again.

195
00:09:10,830 --> 00:09:11,550
Defendant,

196
00:09:12,480 --> 00:09:14,940
you have the right
to make a final statement.

197
00:09:17,720 --> 00:09:19,440
I have more to say.

198
00:09:32,870 --> 00:09:33,600
Prosecutor,

199
00:09:35,080 --> 00:09:36,360
do you really believe

200
00:09:36,990 --> 00:09:38,680
the defendant is guilty?

201
00:09:42,320 --> 00:09:43,640
Why is the indictment

202
00:09:44,150 --> 00:09:46,120
and the listed evidence so simple?

203
00:09:46,670 --> 00:09:47,790
You accuse him

204
00:09:48,030 --> 00:09:49,670
of committing two felonies,

205
00:09:50,000 --> 00:09:52,120
undermining the Strike-Hard Campaign.

206
00:09:52,120 --> 00:09:53,630
The charges are grave.

207
00:09:56,150 --> 00:09:57,400
I remind you—

208
00:10:00,240 --> 00:10:01,480
a guilty verdict

209
00:10:02,230 --> 00:10:04,360
not only deprives a person of freedom.

210
00:10:04,720 --> 00:10:05,670
More importantly,

211
00:10:05,670 --> 00:10:07,330
it strips away their dignity.

212
00:10:11,660 --> 00:10:13,460
The law is a weighty instrument.

213
00:10:14,820 --> 00:10:16,880
We must wield it with the utmost care.

214
00:10:18,170 --> 00:10:20,570
Although our positions in court

215
00:10:20,600 --> 00:10:21,460
are different,

216
00:10:21,550 --> 00:10:23,910
our goal should be the same.

217
00:10:24,440 --> 00:10:25,200
That is,

218
00:10:25,510 --> 00:10:27,080
we hope our country

219
00:10:27,630 --> 00:10:30,000
can bring a sense of security to everyone.

220
00:10:30,370 --> 00:10:31,870
Those who abide by the law

221
00:10:31,890 --> 00:10:33,940
can live without fear.

222
00:10:48,150 --> 00:10:48,720
Please,

223
00:10:49,510 --> 00:10:50,030
no,

224
00:10:52,200 --> 00:10:53,150
I implore you,

225
00:10:54,030 --> 00:10:55,120
stand with us,

226
00:10:55,600 --> 00:10:57,150
and work together

227
00:10:58,720 --> 00:11:00,050
to build such a society.

228
00:11:01,670 --> 00:11:02,270
Thank you.

229
00:11:07,790 --> 00:11:08,510
Order!

230
00:11:09,670 --> 00:11:10,390
Order!

231
00:11:10,410 --> 00:11:11,470
Order in the court!

232
00:11:50,720 --> 00:11:51,320
Who?

233
00:12:57,270 --> 00:12:58,270
Court Pres. Ding.

234
00:12:58,750 --> 00:13:00,320
Why wasn't the verdict delivered in court?

235
00:13:00,320 --> 00:13:01,120
Why?

236
00:13:03,110 --> 00:13:04,370
If I had

237
00:13:04,600 --> 00:13:06,730
delivered the verdict in court today,

238
00:13:07,090 --> 00:13:08,420
I believe the only verdict

239
00:13:08,420 --> 00:13:09,610
would be not guilty.

240
00:13:10,960 --> 00:13:12,440
I've said this before.

241
00:13:13,750 --> 00:13:15,080
But Court Pres. Ding...

242
00:13:16,420 --> 00:13:18,480
You don't need to pass on the message.

243
00:13:28,240 --> 00:13:29,120
Hello, sir.

244
00:13:30,700 --> 00:13:33,850
The reason I didn't deliver the verdict
in court today

245
00:13:34,480 --> 00:13:35,640
is because I believe

246
00:13:36,220 --> 00:13:37,550
he should be acquitted.

247
00:13:38,150 --> 00:13:38,880
Afterwards,

248
00:13:39,120 --> 00:13:40,120
our collegial panel

249
00:13:40,120 --> 00:13:41,180
also had a meeting.

250
00:13:41,510 --> 00:13:42,200
Everyone

251
00:13:42,960 --> 00:13:44,720
agreed with my opinion.

252
00:13:45,200 --> 00:13:46,530
This is also our court's

253
00:13:46,670 --> 00:13:47,670
overall opinion.

254
00:13:48,120 --> 00:13:49,580
I'm reporting this to you.

255
00:13:49,790 --> 00:13:51,000
Is this what you wanted

256
00:13:51,000 --> 00:13:51,600
to tell me?

257
00:13:53,030 --> 00:13:53,870
Nothing else?

258
00:13:54,670 --> 00:13:55,600
Yes, there is.

259
00:13:56,320 --> 00:13:56,910
Sir,

260
00:13:57,360 --> 00:13:58,170
I think

261
00:13:58,750 --> 00:14:00,990
if a person is accused of a crime,

262
00:14:01,790 --> 00:14:03,390
and after the court's trial,

263
00:14:03,870 --> 00:14:06,400
it is determined
that no crime was committed,

264
00:14:06,540 --> 00:14:07,670
and he is acquitted.

265
00:14:08,240 --> 00:14:09,770
That's completely normal.

266
00:14:10,270 --> 00:14:11,910
It's the best

267
00:14:12,320 --> 00:14:15,000
face-saving way out.

268
00:14:15,360 --> 00:14:15,960
Ding,

269
00:14:16,720 --> 00:14:17,840
do you think

270
00:14:17,960 --> 00:14:20,120
I care about my personal reputation?

271
00:14:22,390 --> 00:14:23,940
I don't need a way out.

272
00:14:24,630 --> 00:14:25,920
What I want is to ensure

273
00:14:26,000 --> 00:14:28,000
victory in the fight against crime.

274
00:14:28,080 --> 00:14:29,010
I will fight them

275
00:14:29,080 --> 00:14:30,910
to the very end.

276
00:14:31,790 --> 00:14:32,630
If

277
00:14:33,000 --> 00:14:34,240
you feel the burden is too heavy

278
00:14:34,240 --> 00:14:35,220
and you dare not make the ruling,

279
00:14:35,220 --> 00:14:36,730
then tell me directly!

280
00:14:49,200 --> 00:14:49,800
Zheng.

281
00:14:49,870 --> 00:14:50,440
Yes!

282
00:14:52,320 --> 00:14:53,440
What is it, Court Pres. Ding?

283
00:14:53,440 --> 00:14:54,300
Ask the canteen

284
00:14:54,510 --> 00:14:55,840
to make me a bowl of noodles

285
00:14:55,840 --> 00:14:56,640
with two eggs.

286
00:14:56,790 --> 00:14:57,150
Yes.

287
00:14:57,270 --> 00:14:57,720
No,

288
00:14:58,870 --> 00:14:59,600
make it four.

289
00:15:00,270 --> 00:15:00,870
Four eggs?

290
00:15:01,080 --> 00:15:01,940
How many bowls?

291
00:15:02,270 --> 00:15:02,980
One bowl.

292
00:15:03,000 --> 00:15:03,880
Just me eating.

293
00:15:03,960 --> 00:15:04,630
Alright?

294
00:15:05,720 --> 00:15:06,450
Understood.

295
00:15:06,480 --> 00:15:08,210
One bowl of noodles, four eggs.

296
00:15:18,480 --> 00:15:20,000
Mr. Yuan, are you leaving now?

297
00:15:20,000 --> 00:15:21,200
Not waiting for the verdict?

298
00:15:21,200 --> 00:15:22,130
I'm not waiting.

299
00:15:22,320 --> 00:15:23,600
If we actually win the verdict,

300
00:15:23,600 --> 00:15:24,510
I'd be dancing for joy

301
00:15:24,510 --> 00:15:25,480
right there in court.

302
00:15:25,480 --> 00:15:26,740
That wouldn't be good.

303
00:15:28,010 --> 00:15:28,670
Mr. Yuan,

304
00:15:28,960 --> 00:15:30,670
based on your experience,

305
00:15:30,670 --> 00:15:31,790
when there's no in-court verdict,

306
00:15:31,790 --> 00:15:32,550
does that mean

307
00:15:32,550 --> 00:15:34,350
they're not so sure themselves?

308
00:15:34,750 --> 00:15:36,100
Let's be cautiously optimistic.

309
00:15:36,100 --> 00:15:37,640
I am a pessimistic

310
00:15:37,670 --> 00:15:38,390
optimist.

311
00:15:40,000 --> 00:15:40,840
Anyway,

312
00:15:40,870 --> 00:15:42,200
after witnessing a great debate,

313
00:15:42,200 --> 00:15:43,460
we've all gained a lot.

314
00:15:48,000 --> 00:15:49,030
I'm so happy

315
00:15:49,030 --> 00:15:49,790
to hear that.

316
00:15:50,600 --> 00:15:51,840
It's not that I debated well—

317
00:15:51,840 --> 00:15:53,350
it's just that we're in the right era.

318
00:15:53,350 --> 00:15:54,690
Our national leaders

319
00:15:54,750 --> 00:15:56,750
are pushing hard for the rule of law.

320
00:15:57,480 --> 00:15:58,080
Of course.

321
00:15:58,120 --> 00:16:01,240
building a legal system
cannot be accomplished overnight.

322
00:16:01,240 --> 00:16:02,870
You are witnessing history.

323
00:16:03,670 --> 00:16:05,810
Someday, you can brag about this

324
00:16:05,840 --> 00:16:07,900
to your children and grandchildren.

325
00:16:07,910 --> 00:16:08,600
Mr. Yuan.

326
00:16:09,030 --> 00:16:09,830
Are you saying

327
00:16:10,240 --> 00:16:11,750
we are witnessing history?

328
00:16:11,750 --> 00:16:12,360
Of course.

329
00:16:13,000 --> 00:16:14,320
The progress of the rule of law
isn't something

330
00:16:14,320 --> 00:16:15,510
that depends on just one person.

331
00:16:15,510 --> 00:16:16,120
Mr. Yuan.

332
00:16:16,960 --> 00:16:17,670
Mr. Yuan.

333
00:16:18,490 --> 00:16:19,180
Mr. Yuan.

334
00:16:19,240 --> 00:16:19,790
Mr. Qin.

335
00:16:20,510 --> 00:16:21,120
Mr. Qin.

336
00:16:21,150 --> 00:16:22,000
You are

337
00:16:22,000 --> 00:16:23,400
a very excellent lawyer.

338
00:16:23,960 --> 00:16:25,150
Your performance in court

339
00:16:25,150 --> 00:16:25,910
was amazing.

340
00:16:26,390 --> 00:16:28,150
It was a pleasure working with you.

341
00:16:28,150 --> 00:16:29,440
I hope we have the chance

342
00:16:29,440 --> 00:16:30,770
to work together again.

343
00:16:30,960 --> 00:16:32,560
That's exactly why I'm here.

344
00:16:32,880 --> 00:16:34,550
I want to go back to Beijing with you—

345
00:16:34,550 --> 00:16:36,080
to work with you long‑term.

346
00:16:36,460 --> 00:16:37,590
I've made up my mind.

347
00:16:37,840 --> 00:16:39,690
I'll go to Beijing to work for you.

348
00:16:39,690 --> 00:16:41,150
The salary doesn't matter.

349
00:16:41,150 --> 00:16:42,150
As long as I'm fed.

350
00:16:42,910 --> 00:16:44,370
Even if I'm not, it's fine.

351
00:16:44,750 --> 00:16:45,360
This time,

352
00:16:45,670 --> 00:16:47,080
I went through a test.

353
00:16:47,440 --> 00:16:47,790
Yes.

354
00:16:47,790 --> 00:16:48,520
You also said

355
00:16:48,550 --> 00:16:49,950
I'm an excellent lawyer.

356
00:16:50,320 --> 00:16:50,960
Mr. Yuan.

357
00:16:51,030 --> 00:16:52,440
The bus is arriving soon.

358
00:16:52,440 --> 00:16:53,630
We're running out of time.

359
00:16:53,630 --> 00:16:54,030
Yes.

360
00:16:54,050 --> 00:16:54,550
Well,

361
00:16:54,570 --> 00:16:55,160
Mr. Qin,

362
00:16:55,360 --> 00:16:56,480
I'll think about it.

363
00:16:56,480 --> 00:16:58,120
I'm in a hurry now.

364
00:16:58,600 --> 00:16:59,130
Mr. Yuan.

365
00:16:59,280 --> 00:17:00,270
I bought the tickets.

366
00:17:00,270 --> 00:17:00,840
Three of them.

367
00:17:00,840 --> 00:17:02,320
I'll go to the provincial capital
with you.

368
00:17:02,320 --> 00:17:03,390
We can talk on the train.

369
00:17:03,390 --> 00:17:03,990
Everyone.

370
00:17:04,030 --> 00:17:05,000
No need to see us off.

371
00:17:05,000 --> 00:17:05,589
Goodbye.

372
00:17:05,720 --> 00:17:06,400
Let's go.

373
00:17:06,960 --> 00:17:07,750
Off we go.

374
00:17:08,170 --> 00:17:08,849
Mr. Qin.

375
00:17:08,880 --> 00:17:09,640
This isn't something

376
00:17:09,640 --> 00:17:10,200
Mr. Yuan can decide alone.

377
00:17:10,200 --> 00:17:11,060
Don't touch me!

378
00:17:12,160 --> 00:17:13,089
I'm sorry, Mr. Yuan.

379
00:17:13,089 --> 00:17:14,589
That wasn't directed at you.

380
00:17:14,589 --> 00:17:16,160
I can work hard.

381
00:17:16,349 --> 00:17:17,440
I can do anything.

382
00:17:18,000 --> 00:17:19,599
Errands, filing documents,

383
00:17:19,680 --> 00:17:20,640
running deliveries—whatever.

384
00:17:20,640 --> 00:17:21,440
Wait, well...

385
00:17:31,240 --> 00:17:32,770
Hitting people is illegal.

386
00:17:34,300 --> 00:17:35,360
Hitting people...

387
00:17:38,730 --> 00:17:40,260
Hitting people is illegal.

388
00:17:40,980 --> 00:17:42,350
Let's hurry up and go.

389
00:17:45,480 --> 00:17:46,270
Which way?

390
00:17:46,290 --> 00:17:47,160
Well, this way.

391
00:17:57,240 --> 00:17:58,400
Come on.

392
00:17:59,570 --> 00:18:00,440
Take a big bite.

393
00:18:03,470 --> 00:18:04,960
Oh man, I'm starving.

394
00:18:04,980 --> 00:18:05,710
I haven't had

395
00:18:06,110 --> 00:18:07,310
a proper meal all day.

396
00:18:07,310 --> 00:18:09,410
You are not the one defending,
why are you nervous?

397
00:18:09,410 --> 00:18:10,350
I'm quite nervous too,

398
00:18:10,350 --> 00:18:12,210
so nervous that my stomach hurts.

399
00:18:14,920 --> 00:18:17,780
I don't think Mr. Yuan
can make much of a difference.

400
00:18:19,240 --> 00:18:20,170
What do you mean?

401
00:18:21,400 --> 00:18:22,460
He said it himself,

402
00:18:22,790 --> 00:18:24,400
if this matter is resolved in the end,

403
00:18:24,400 --> 00:18:25,680
it's because the higher-ups
take it seriously,

404
00:18:25,680 --> 00:18:27,340
not because he defended well.

405
00:18:29,270 --> 00:18:30,300
I agree with you.

406
00:18:30,640 --> 00:18:32,030
We should just do nothing

407
00:18:32,030 --> 00:18:33,720
and wait for pies to fall from the sky.

408
00:18:33,720 --> 00:18:34,720
And when seven of them drop,

409
00:18:34,720 --> 00:18:36,090
we only eat the seventh one.

410
00:18:36,090 --> 00:18:37,160
Pat our bellies when we're done—

411
00:18:37,160 --> 00:18:37,640
full.

412
00:18:38,270 --> 00:18:39,880
I wasn't saying anything bad
about Mr. Yuan.

413
00:18:39,880 --> 00:18:41,440
You have no right to say that about him.

414
00:18:41,440 --> 00:18:42,240
What I mean is,

415
00:18:42,960 --> 00:18:44,440
grassroots efforts from the bottom up

416
00:18:44,440 --> 00:18:45,270
can never match

417
00:18:45,270 --> 00:18:47,000
the impact of top-down reform.

418
00:18:50,170 --> 00:18:52,230
But without this year of internship,

419
00:18:52,790 --> 00:18:53,790
we'd never have known

420
00:18:53,790 --> 00:18:55,920
where the real problems actually lie.

421
00:18:58,270 --> 00:19:00,070
I'm not trying to debate you, Yu.

422
00:19:00,070 --> 00:19:01,270
-Chen Yizhong.
-I...

423
00:19:02,680 --> 00:19:03,960
Long-distance call from Beijing.

424
00:19:03,960 --> 00:19:04,440
Okay.

425
00:19:21,640 --> 00:19:22,270
Mr. Qin.

426
00:19:24,790 --> 00:19:25,480
Mr. Yuan

427
00:19:25,670 --> 00:19:27,160
has already left, right?

428
00:19:28,750 --> 00:19:29,350
He's gone,

429
00:19:29,790 --> 00:19:30,680
but he didn't go back to Beijing.

430
00:19:30,680 --> 00:19:32,480
He went to Chengdu for business.

431
00:19:33,160 --> 00:19:34,480
Are you okay?

432
00:19:35,350 --> 00:19:35,960
I'm fine.

433
00:19:38,160 --> 00:19:39,160
I just came to ask.

434
00:19:40,270 --> 00:19:41,400
Good that he's gone.

435
00:19:46,640 --> 00:19:48,920
I was just daydreaming anyway.

436
00:19:50,750 --> 00:19:51,440
Mr. Qin.

437
00:20:04,180 --> 00:20:05,780
Hello, this is Chen Yizhong.

438
00:20:05,960 --> 00:20:06,890
Is that Yizhong?

439
00:20:07,590 --> 00:20:08,880
Who do you think I am?

440
00:20:09,550 --> 00:20:10,270
Mr. Cheng.

441
00:20:10,730 --> 00:20:11,830
This is the call for me.

442
00:20:11,830 --> 00:20:12,880
Yizhong, listen—

443
00:20:12,900 --> 00:20:13,830
there's a result

444
00:20:13,960 --> 00:20:14,830
for that case.

445
00:20:15,240 --> 00:20:16,830
The leadership has issued a directive:

446
00:20:16,830 --> 00:20:18,200
this is a serious case

447
00:20:18,270 --> 00:20:20,330
of illegality and unconstitutionality.

448
00:20:20,330 --> 00:20:22,180
It must be supervised and rectified.

449
00:20:22,180 --> 00:20:22,750
Hold on.

450
00:20:23,680 --> 00:20:24,480
They also said

451
00:20:24,830 --> 00:20:26,350
this is a typical case

452
00:20:26,350 --> 00:20:27,500
of the National People's Congress

453
00:20:27,500 --> 00:20:28,510
fulfilling its supervisory function.

454
00:20:28,510 --> 00:20:28,980
And then... Right.

455
00:20:28,980 --> 00:20:29,490
Wait.

456
00:20:30,830 --> 00:20:33,030
The directive has already been issued.

457
00:20:33,350 --> 00:20:34,800
It may have already

458
00:20:34,860 --> 00:20:37,190
-It must have arrived.
-arrived in Nanyu.

459
00:20:37,480 --> 00:20:38,000
Really?

460
00:20:38,200 --> 00:20:39,000
That's great.

461
00:20:40,070 --> 00:20:41,070
How was the trial?

462
00:20:41,410 --> 00:20:42,480
The great Mr. Yuan

463
00:20:42,590 --> 00:20:45,050
truly lived up to his reputation,
didn't he?

464
00:20:45,070 --> 00:20:46,470
Mr. Yuan argued very well

465
00:20:46,680 --> 00:20:47,750
and helped us a lot.

466
00:20:48,240 --> 00:20:50,700
And the presiding judge
and the prosecutors

467
00:20:51,070 --> 00:20:52,870
actually agree in their hearts.

468
00:20:52,880 --> 00:20:54,250
And that Mr. Qin.

469
00:20:55,070 --> 00:20:56,930
Mr. Qin also performed very well.

470
00:21:00,720 --> 00:21:01,350
Well.

471
00:21:02,000 --> 00:21:02,640
Mr. Cheng.

472
00:21:03,000 --> 00:21:04,800
Something's come up. I gotta go.

473
00:21:05,040 --> 00:21:05,650
Yizhong.

474
00:21:05,680 --> 00:21:06,680
Let's talk later.

475
00:21:24,160 --> 00:21:24,750
Mr. Qin.

476
00:21:25,400 --> 00:21:26,110
Mr. Qin.

477
00:21:30,160 --> 00:21:30,830
Qin Zhigao,

478
00:21:31,200 --> 00:21:32,600
where were you assigned?

479
00:21:33,400 --> 00:21:35,200
The provincial procuratorate.

480
00:21:35,310 --> 00:21:36,370
Congratulations.

481
00:21:37,960 --> 00:21:38,830
Then,

482
00:21:39,480 --> 00:21:40,610
we have to part ways.

483
00:21:41,160 --> 00:21:42,490
Remember to wait for me.

484
00:21:44,720 --> 00:21:46,320
After you graduate in a year,

485
00:21:46,590 --> 00:21:49,400
can you also be assigned back
to the provincial capital?

486
00:21:49,400 --> 00:21:50,160
I don't know.

487
00:21:52,160 --> 00:21:54,760
I'll follow
the organization's arrangement.

488
00:21:57,510 --> 00:21:59,510
Do you also hope I get assigned back?

489
00:21:59,750 --> 00:22:00,240
Yes.

490
00:22:01,110 --> 00:22:02,550
I want to work with you,

491
00:22:03,440 --> 00:22:04,970
and keep working together.

492
00:22:08,920 --> 00:22:09,920
I have to go back.

493
00:22:11,480 --> 00:22:12,680
Remember to write to me.

494
00:22:12,680 --> 00:22:13,200
Okay.

495
00:22:14,070 --> 00:22:15,640
Zhao Xiulan.

496
00:22:16,310 --> 00:22:17,590
Room 108, Building 19.

497
00:22:27,830 --> 00:22:28,550
Qin Zhigao,

498
00:22:29,920 --> 00:22:31,250
wait for me to graduate.

499
00:22:34,110 --> 00:22:34,680
Goodbye.

500
00:22:47,550 --> 00:22:48,270
So,

501
00:22:49,210 --> 00:22:51,010
did you wait for her to graduate?

502
00:22:54,160 --> 00:22:54,920
Actually,

503
00:22:57,110 --> 00:22:59,000
I already had a wife back then.

504
00:23:00,260 --> 00:23:02,710
She's the one you saw

505
00:23:02,790 --> 00:23:04,850
that day at the guesthouse entrance.

506
00:23:04,920 --> 00:23:05,920
I know. I know.

507
00:23:09,200 --> 00:23:11,130
Did you ever see Zhao Xiulan again?

508
00:23:11,920 --> 00:23:12,590
No.

509
00:23:13,830 --> 00:23:14,760
I didn't dare to.

510
00:23:17,550 --> 00:23:18,590
I was too ashamed.

511
00:23:20,720 --> 00:23:22,250
Every time I mentioned her,

512
00:23:23,310 --> 00:23:25,070
my wife would get upset.

513
00:23:29,070 --> 00:23:30,130
The procuratorate

514
00:23:30,160 --> 00:23:33,000
was afraid she'd keep making a scene
and cause a bad impression.

515
00:23:33,000 --> 00:23:33,800
So they simply

516
00:23:34,640 --> 00:23:36,170
sent me back to my hometown.

517
00:23:36,720 --> 00:23:37,640
I had no choice

518
00:23:38,550 --> 00:23:40,960
but to teach at the middle school in town.

519
00:23:41,960 --> 00:23:44,560
And you've been living like that
all this time?

520
00:23:45,550 --> 00:23:46,590
I deserved it.

521
00:23:48,070 --> 00:23:49,200
It was retribution.

522
00:23:51,640 --> 00:23:53,100
Did she hate you that much?

523
00:23:54,400 --> 00:23:55,240
Hate me?

524
00:23:56,750 --> 00:23:58,950
When I was sent down to the countryside,

525
00:23:59,400 --> 00:24:01,750
she stayed by my side the whole time.

526
00:24:03,960 --> 00:24:05,310
When I was dying,

527
00:24:05,640 --> 00:24:06,550
she dragged me

528
00:24:06,580 --> 00:24:08,710
for miles to see a doctor.

529
00:24:12,290 --> 00:24:13,220
Please save him.

530
00:24:13,240 --> 00:24:13,750
Please save him.

531
00:24:13,750 --> 00:24:14,440
No.

532
00:24:14,440 --> 00:24:15,110
We really can't.

533
00:24:15,110 --> 00:24:16,090
-It's hospital policy.
-Please!

534
00:24:16,090 --> 00:24:16,960
It's hospital policy.

535
00:24:16,960 --> 00:24:18,090
I'll give you money.

536
00:24:18,160 --> 00:24:19,890
No way, the hospital has rules.

537
00:24:20,240 --> 00:24:21,270
Wait.

538
00:24:22,140 --> 00:24:23,630
Please, give him the medicine first.

539
00:24:23,630 --> 00:24:24,750
Save his life first, please.

540
00:24:24,750 --> 00:24:25,680
Please, doctor.

541
00:24:25,750 --> 00:24:27,210
Please, doctor.

542
00:24:27,790 --> 00:24:29,170
To pay for my treatment—

543
00:24:29,750 --> 00:24:31,750
just for 2,000 yuan in bride price,

544
00:24:32,000 --> 00:24:34,200
she forced our daughter into marriage.

545
00:24:36,830 --> 00:24:37,440
Later,

546
00:24:39,550 --> 00:24:40,880
I got my job back

547
00:24:42,030 --> 00:24:43,830
and joined the advisory office.

548
00:24:44,000 --> 00:24:45,930
I brought her to the county as well.

549
00:24:46,920 --> 00:24:47,830
She had no job.

550
00:24:49,200 --> 00:24:50,930
Every day at the intersection,

551
00:24:51,030 --> 00:24:51,960
she sold peanuts

552
00:24:53,270 --> 00:24:54,800
to help support the family.

553
00:24:54,960 --> 00:24:56,820
Every morning, she got up at four.

554
00:24:57,920 --> 00:24:59,880
The skin on her hands peeled off,

555
00:25:00,640 --> 00:25:01,750
but she wouldn't even

556
00:25:01,750 --> 00:25:03,210
wear a pair of work gloves.

557
00:25:04,030 --> 00:25:04,790
Peanuts.

558
00:25:06,350 --> 00:25:06,790
Okay.

559
00:25:08,550 --> 00:25:09,160
What?

560
00:25:14,480 --> 00:25:15,240
Little brat.

561
00:25:15,790 --> 00:25:16,760
Freeloader!

562
00:25:17,790 --> 00:25:19,120
Do you think she hates me

563
00:25:20,310 --> 00:25:21,400
or cares about me?

564
00:25:23,880 --> 00:25:25,160
I can't say for sure.

565
00:25:26,160 --> 00:25:28,480
Maybe she just can't leave you.

566
00:25:29,310 --> 00:25:30,160
In the end,

567
00:25:32,310 --> 00:25:33,590
we'll die together.

568
00:25:34,760 --> 00:25:36,760
Ashes to ashes, dust to dust.

569
00:25:37,640 --> 00:25:39,440
The only one I can't let go of,

570
00:25:40,440 --> 00:25:41,840
the only one I've failed,

571
00:25:43,200 --> 00:25:44,880
is our Xiaowen.

572
00:25:48,000 --> 00:25:49,440
So your daughter

573
00:25:49,440 --> 00:25:52,040
has always had a bad relationship
with you two?

574
00:25:55,640 --> 00:25:58,000
She has every right to hate us.

575
00:25:59,590 --> 00:26:01,190
Have you ever looked for her?

576
00:26:03,030 --> 00:26:04,690
It wouldn't help even if I did.

577
00:26:10,640 --> 00:26:11,240
Yizhong.

578
00:26:13,000 --> 00:26:14,000
I've only told you

579
00:26:14,110 --> 00:26:15,680
about this matter.

580
00:26:16,350 --> 00:26:17,550
If you tell anyone, I will...

581
00:26:17,550 --> 00:26:18,520
Don't worry.

582
00:26:18,680 --> 00:26:20,080
I definitely won't tell.

583
00:26:20,160 --> 00:26:20,690
Trust me.

584
00:26:26,590 --> 00:26:27,270
Yizhong.

585
00:26:30,200 --> 00:26:32,000
This was my last chance

586
00:26:33,880 --> 00:26:36,350
to start my life over.

587
00:26:41,000 --> 00:26:41,600
It's gone.

588
00:26:47,310 --> 00:26:48,550
But I have no regrets.

589
00:26:51,240 --> 00:26:52,770
I went back to my alma mater,

590
00:26:54,350 --> 00:26:56,440
saw Room 108 in Building 19,

591
00:26:58,920 --> 00:27:01,400
and finally stood tall

592
00:27:03,350 --> 00:27:04,550
as a true lawyer.

593
00:27:06,310 --> 00:27:08,510
For the first time in over twenty years,

594
00:27:08,590 --> 00:27:10,750
I held my head high.

595
00:27:12,720 --> 00:27:14,120
I can die without regret.

596
00:27:22,070 --> 00:27:22,680
Yizhong.

597
00:27:23,400 --> 00:27:25,000
Thank you for saving my life.

598
00:27:55,000 --> 00:27:56,530
That is not bad, right, sir?

599
00:27:56,640 --> 00:27:58,600
No verdict has been issued yet anyway.

600
00:27:58,600 --> 00:27:59,910
So our court can just

601
00:28:00,070 --> 00:28:01,330
hold another session,

602
00:28:01,480 --> 00:28:02,550
find him not guilty,

603
00:28:02,550 --> 00:28:03,950
and release him in court.

604
00:28:04,310 --> 00:28:06,400
Wait,
they undermined the Strike-Hard Campaign.

605
00:28:06,400 --> 00:28:08,440
Even if it doesn't constitute a crime,

606
00:28:08,440 --> 00:28:10,970
it doesn't mean
we arrested the wrong people.

607
00:28:12,310 --> 00:28:12,790
Right?

608
00:28:13,270 --> 00:28:13,730
This...

609
00:28:15,640 --> 00:28:16,550
This

610
00:28:17,070 --> 00:28:18,880
is not easy to handle.

611
00:28:22,680 --> 00:28:23,510
Come on, Ding,

612
00:28:24,380 --> 00:28:25,990
do you really have to

613
00:28:26,020 --> 00:28:27,460
embarrass us like this?

614
00:28:27,960 --> 00:28:28,400
No.

615
00:28:29,720 --> 00:28:31,940
Court Pres. Ding once proposed a concept

616
00:28:31,940 --> 00:28:34,140
called "exemption from prosecution."

617
00:28:34,290 --> 00:28:35,400
Wait, exemption from prosecution?

618
00:28:35,400 --> 00:28:37,840
How is that any different
from an acquittal?

619
00:28:37,840 --> 00:28:38,840
An acquittal means

620
00:28:38,840 --> 00:28:40,500
we arrested the wrong person.

621
00:28:40,860 --> 00:28:43,640
Exemption from prosecution means
we got the right person,

622
00:28:43,640 --> 00:28:45,370
but since the offense is minor,

623
00:28:45,830 --> 00:28:47,200
we simply choose not to pursue charges.

624
00:28:47,200 --> 00:28:48,530
Well, this approach...

625
00:28:48,660 --> 00:28:50,710
Before the trial,

626
00:28:51,070 --> 00:28:52,270
it might have worked.

627
00:28:52,730 --> 00:28:54,050
But now, sir,

628
00:28:54,400 --> 00:28:56,000
the document has already come down.

629
00:28:56,000 --> 00:28:56,830
I'm afraid...

630
00:29:02,030 --> 00:29:02,680
All right.

631
00:29:04,270 --> 00:29:05,200
Let's just do it.

632
00:29:06,880 --> 00:29:08,480
Exemption from prosecution

633
00:29:08,550 --> 00:29:09,030
right?

634
00:29:10,830 --> 00:29:11,560
Release him.

635
00:29:12,550 --> 00:29:13,200
Release!

636
00:29:14,640 --> 00:29:15,030
Okay.

637
00:29:15,350 --> 00:29:16,310
Okay.

638
00:29:16,720 --> 00:29:17,480
Well...

639
00:29:17,510 --> 00:29:18,390
Then we'll be leaving first.

640
00:29:18,390 --> 00:29:19,300
Okay, Ding.

641
00:29:19,720 --> 00:29:20,050
Okay.

642
00:29:29,270 --> 00:29:29,880
Comrade,

643
00:29:30,270 --> 00:29:31,410
where are we going?

644
00:29:31,950 --> 00:29:33,680
Don't I need to wear handcuffs?

645
00:29:33,880 --> 00:29:35,110
Just walk, don't ask.

646
00:29:39,510 --> 00:29:40,370
Director Hong.

647
00:29:43,640 --> 00:29:45,240
Do you know what this is about?

648
00:29:45,240 --> 00:29:45,750
No.

649
00:29:46,590 --> 00:29:48,110
Probably good news.

650
00:29:48,510 --> 00:29:48,970
Really?

651
00:29:51,510 --> 00:29:52,070
That day,

652
00:29:52,310 --> 00:29:54,030
why did they interrogate you first?

653
00:29:54,030 --> 00:29:55,030
I'm the director.

654
00:29:55,270 --> 00:29:57,730
They really don't treat me
like an official.

655
00:30:07,200 --> 00:30:07,860
Have a seat.

656
00:30:14,440 --> 00:30:15,900
Hong Zhansheng, Li Xiang,

657
00:30:16,140 --> 00:30:17,500
the procuratorate has reviewed your case.

658
00:30:17,500 --> 00:30:18,850
After review,

659
00:30:19,200 --> 00:30:20,310
it is determined

660
00:30:20,720 --> 00:30:21,790
that your criminal conduct

661
00:30:21,790 --> 00:30:23,050
was relatively minor.

662
00:30:24,000 --> 00:30:26,600
Your attitude of confession
was cooperative.

663
00:30:26,630 --> 00:30:27,470
You are free.

664
00:30:30,750 --> 00:30:31,810
You can go back now.

665
00:30:32,480 --> 00:30:33,280
You mean

666
00:30:33,310 --> 00:30:34,710
we can go home now, right?

667
00:30:34,790 --> 00:30:35,310
Yes.

668
00:30:36,260 --> 00:30:37,400
Comrade, let me tell you...

669
00:30:37,400 --> 00:30:38,270
Director, wait a minute.

670
00:30:38,270 --> 00:30:39,530
Wait, wait, Director.

671
00:30:39,880 --> 00:30:40,410
Comrade.

672
00:30:41,680 --> 00:30:43,000
You just said

673
00:30:44,030 --> 00:30:45,160
that our criminal conduct

674
00:30:45,160 --> 00:30:46,590
was relatively minor,

675
00:30:46,650 --> 00:30:47,890
so you have made

676
00:30:47,920 --> 00:30:48,960
a decision not to pursue charges,

677
00:30:48,960 --> 00:30:49,400
right?

678
00:30:49,830 --> 00:30:50,400
Yes.

679
00:30:54,030 --> 00:30:55,230
Then I'm not leaving.

680
00:30:59,310 --> 00:31:00,370
What are you doing?

681
00:31:00,720 --> 00:31:02,250
They are letting us go back.

682
00:31:02,480 --> 00:31:03,270
How about you explain the law to me?

683
00:31:03,270 --> 00:31:04,200
What do you mean?

684
00:31:04,200 --> 00:31:04,800
Director.

685
00:31:05,510 --> 00:31:06,710
Not pursuing charges

686
00:31:06,750 --> 00:31:08,800
means we did commit a crime,

687
00:31:08,830 --> 00:31:10,680
but given the minor circumstances,

688
00:31:10,680 --> 00:31:11,810
the procuratorate,

689
00:31:11,830 --> 00:31:12,880
in its leniency,

690
00:31:13,400 --> 00:31:14,060
has decided

691
00:31:14,270 --> 00:31:16,130
not to pursue charges against us.

692
00:31:23,310 --> 00:31:24,240
Hong Zhansheng,

693
00:31:24,240 --> 00:31:24,920
Li Xiang,

694
00:31:25,490 --> 00:31:26,830
we have studied your case

695
00:31:26,830 --> 00:31:27,720
multiple times

696
00:31:28,000 --> 00:31:30,930
and have carefully made this decision
not to pursue.

697
00:31:31,070 --> 00:31:33,200
This is your chance to regain freedom.

698
00:31:33,350 --> 00:31:34,480
So we hope you

699
00:31:34,830 --> 00:31:35,550
cherish it.

700
00:31:37,480 --> 00:31:38,270
Comrade,

701
00:31:38,470 --> 00:31:39,330
I don't need it.

702
00:31:39,510 --> 00:31:40,310
I am innocent.

703
00:31:40,590 --> 00:31:42,250
I do not accept this decision.

704
00:31:42,440 --> 00:31:43,170
Take me back.

705
00:31:45,000 --> 00:31:45,640
Li Xiang.

706
00:31:46,240 --> 00:31:47,300
What are you doing?

707
00:31:47,440 --> 00:31:48,200
You are a lawyer.

708
00:31:48,200 --> 00:31:49,730
How can you be so imprecise?

709
00:31:51,310 --> 00:31:52,370
Take us both back.

710
00:31:57,830 --> 00:31:59,030
They've gone too far!

711
00:32:00,600 --> 00:32:02,240
When the Central Working Group arrives,

712
00:32:02,240 --> 00:32:03,110
just tell them—

713
00:32:04,240 --> 00:32:06,170
they refused to leave on their own.

714
00:32:07,550 --> 00:32:08,950
Let them stay in the cell.

715
00:32:11,920 --> 00:32:12,920
Court Pres. Ding, I'll do it.

716
00:32:12,920 --> 00:32:13,350
I'll do it.

717
00:32:13,350 --> 00:32:14,050
Don't you touch it.

718
00:32:14,050 --> 00:32:14,810
Let me do it.

719
00:32:17,480 --> 00:32:18,260
I am getting old.

720
00:32:18,260 --> 00:32:20,070
Getting up suddenly makes me dizzy.

721
00:32:20,070 --> 00:32:21,310
Sit down and rest a while.

722
00:32:21,310 --> 00:32:22,110
Once the working group arrives,

723
00:32:22,110 --> 00:32:24,510
we will be in an even more
passive position.

724
00:32:24,640 --> 00:32:26,240
No, what is going on now?

725
00:32:27,000 --> 00:32:29,530
I was locked up for five or six years
back then.

726
00:32:30,030 --> 00:32:31,560
I was also wrongly accused.

727
00:32:32,350 --> 00:32:32,960
Also?

728
00:32:36,930 --> 00:32:38,720
Leader has also been wrongly accused.

729
00:32:38,720 --> 00:32:40,400
Don't nitpick my words.

730
00:32:40,750 --> 00:32:41,960
What I mean is,

731
00:32:42,490 --> 00:32:43,960
after the organization talked to me,

732
00:32:43,960 --> 00:32:45,030
they let me out.

733
00:32:45,440 --> 00:32:47,640
But I never uttered a single complaint.

734
00:32:48,680 --> 00:32:50,350
It's like a mother beating her child—

735
00:32:50,350 --> 00:32:52,110
sure, sometimes she gets it wrong,

736
00:32:52,110 --> 00:32:54,170
but after all, she's still my mother.

737
00:32:56,480 --> 00:32:57,070
Sir.

738
00:32:57,510 --> 00:32:58,750
A mother beating her child,

739
00:32:58,750 --> 00:33:00,110
that is your understanding.

740
00:33:00,110 --> 00:33:01,570
As for our understanding,

741
00:33:01,680 --> 00:33:02,680
Communists

742
00:33:02,790 --> 00:33:04,830
should seek truth from facts

743
00:33:04,960 --> 00:33:06,960
and admit mistakes when they're wrong.

744
00:33:06,960 --> 00:33:07,510
Sorry.

745
00:33:07,750 --> 00:33:08,810
I am not feeling well.

746
00:33:08,810 --> 00:33:09,790
I'll leave first.

747
00:33:09,790 --> 00:33:11,240
You two continue.

748
00:33:12,830 --> 00:33:14,350
I have a headache.

749
00:33:15,550 --> 00:33:16,920
I'll go back first.

750
00:33:17,550 --> 00:33:18,030
Ding.

751
00:33:18,240 --> 00:33:19,590
What? What do you mean?

752
00:33:22,170 --> 00:33:23,350
If you have problems or opinions,

753
00:33:23,350 --> 00:33:24,410
just bring them up.

754
00:33:25,160 --> 00:33:25,750
In accordance with

755
00:33:25,750 --> 00:33:29,200
Article 120 of the Criminal Procedure Law

756
00:33:29,680 --> 00:33:31,720
of the People's Republic of China,

757
00:33:32,110 --> 00:33:33,640
the judgment is as follows:

758
00:33:33,880 --> 00:33:35,750
The defendants, Hong Zhansheng

759
00:33:36,070 --> 00:33:36,920
and Li Xiang

760
00:33:37,400 --> 00:33:38,260
are acquitted!

761
00:33:40,510 --> 00:33:41,160
Good!

762
00:33:43,790 --> 00:33:45,960
After three years
of the Strike-Hard Campaign,

763
00:33:45,960 --> 00:33:48,590
the national public security
has improved significantly.

764
00:33:48,590 --> 00:33:49,810
Social stability was restored,

765
00:33:49,810 --> 00:33:52,930
and the environment
for reform and opening-up was secured.

766
00:33:52,930 --> 00:33:55,250
These achievements were made
by the leadership of the Party

767
00:33:55,250 --> 00:33:57,130
and the concerted efforts of the masses

768
00:33:57,130 --> 00:33:58,790
and political-legal organs.

769
00:33:58,920 --> 00:33:59,550
However,

770
00:33:59,830 --> 00:34:01,590
due to historical limitations,

771
00:34:01,590 --> 00:34:03,640
the Strike-Hard Campaign
prioritized expediency in case handling

772
00:34:03,640 --> 00:34:05,770
at the expense of procedural justice.

773
00:34:05,960 --> 00:34:07,440
Legal application was ambiguous,

774
00:34:07,440 --> 00:34:09,170
sentencing standards were rigid,

775
00:34:09,170 --> 00:34:11,880
and safeguards for human rights
and the rule of law were inadequate.

776
00:34:11,880 --> 00:34:12,540
Since then,

777
00:34:12,880 --> 00:34:14,480
China has drawn lessons
from this experience,

778
00:34:14,480 --> 00:34:16,880
strictly implemented the principles
of Nullum Crimen Sine Lege

779
00:34:16,880 --> 00:34:19,719
and suiting punishment to the crime
and criminal responsibility,

780
00:34:19,719 --> 00:34:21,260
refined systems
such as death penalty review

781
00:34:21,260 --> 00:34:22,449
and legal defense,

782
00:34:22,960 --> 00:34:24,400
abolished the crime of hooliganism,

783
00:34:24,400 --> 00:34:26,510
public parading of criminals,
and re-education through labor,

784
00:34:26,510 --> 00:34:31,170
and promoted a comprehensive transition
to the rule of law in criminal governance.

785
00:34:37,320 --> 00:34:37,840
Hello.

786
00:34:38,230 --> 00:34:39,429
It's me, Su Guosheng.

787
00:34:41,070 --> 00:34:42,510
I made a grave mistake.

788
00:34:43,960 --> 00:34:44,840
This is a classic case of

789
00:34:44,840 --> 00:34:46,170
bureaucratic conduct.

790
00:34:46,590 --> 00:34:47,510
Communists

791
00:34:47,710 --> 00:34:50,280
must adhere to the principle
of seeking truth from facts.

792
00:34:50,280 --> 00:34:52,710
The Party Central Committee places
great emphasis on legal development.

793
00:34:52,710 --> 00:34:53,510
Your behavior

794
00:34:53,710 --> 00:34:55,480
has seriously violated discipline,

795
00:34:55,480 --> 00:34:56,880
and you must be punished.

796
00:34:57,840 --> 00:34:59,440
I'll hand over

797
00:34:59,440 --> 00:35:01,170
all my work as soon as possible.

798
00:35:01,230 --> 00:35:02,590
And report to the study class

799
00:35:02,590 --> 00:35:04,060
as early as possible.

800
00:35:13,760 --> 00:35:15,420
I haven't packed my stuff yet.

801
00:35:16,510 --> 00:35:17,920
Then hurry up and pack.

802
00:35:17,960 --> 00:35:18,900
Go back and hurry.

803
00:35:18,900 --> 00:35:19,630
Zhang Lihui.

804
00:35:22,700 --> 00:35:23,550
Keep it brief.

805
00:35:25,640 --> 00:35:28,040
What's the matter, Jianmin, something up?

806
00:35:28,150 --> 00:35:29,480
I heard you're leaving.

807
00:35:29,550 --> 00:35:30,750
I came to say goodbye.

808
00:35:31,280 --> 00:35:31,920
Yes.

809
00:35:32,680 --> 00:35:33,400
Thank you.

810
00:35:33,550 --> 00:35:34,380
If you didn't come to me,

811
00:35:34,380 --> 00:35:36,150
I would've gone to you to say goodbye.

812
00:35:36,150 --> 00:35:36,710
Really?

813
00:35:39,510 --> 00:35:40,110
Yes.

814
00:35:42,450 --> 00:35:43,640
Thank you for

815
00:35:43,670 --> 00:35:45,360
taking care of us so well this past year.

816
00:35:45,360 --> 00:35:46,160
It was my duty.

817
00:35:46,960 --> 00:35:47,510
My duty.

818
00:35:49,570 --> 00:35:50,190
Right,

819
00:35:56,710 --> 00:35:58,020
you gave me a book last time.

820
00:35:58,020 --> 00:35:59,350
I forgot to pay you.

821
00:35:59,710 --> 00:36:00,320
No need.

822
00:36:00,800 --> 00:36:01,320
No need.

823
00:36:01,590 --> 00:36:02,760
That book was a gift.

824
00:36:03,670 --> 00:36:04,730
Lihui, ready to go?

825
00:36:07,400 --> 00:36:09,110
We're taking the first bus tomorrow,

826
00:36:09,110 --> 00:36:09,840
very early.

827
00:36:10,150 --> 00:36:11,010
Now that we are parting ways,

828
00:36:11,010 --> 00:36:12,600
who knows when

829
00:36:12,630 --> 00:36:14,160
we'll be able to meet again.

830
00:36:15,840 --> 00:36:17,170
Let's say goodbye here.

831
00:36:22,480 --> 00:36:23,030
Goodbye.

832
00:36:22,900 --> 00:36:28,200
♪ We bid farewell,
yet time won't turn back ♪

833
00:36:25,360 --> 00:36:26,400
I'll always remember

834
00:36:26,400 --> 00:36:27,800
your encouraging words.

835
00:36:30,150 --> 00:36:31,320
If you ever need me,

836
00:36:30,560 --> 00:36:36,130
♪ Cherish youth still,
it flows into the vast tide ♪

837
00:36:31,960 --> 00:36:33,290
for anything, anytime,

838
00:36:33,400 --> 00:36:34,400
you can come to me.

839
00:36:38,350 --> 00:36:38,950
I'm leaving then.

840
00:36:38,420 --> 00:36:46,500
♪ Let's vow to head
for our separate paths ♪

841
00:36:39,510 --> 00:36:40,070
Goodbye.

842
00:36:40,550 --> 00:36:41,080
Goodbye.

843
00:36:42,760 --> 00:36:43,440
Remember,

844
00:36:45,110 --> 00:36:46,590
anything, anytime.

845
00:36:46,680 --> 00:36:51,920
♪ Yet guard the same dream deep inside ♪

846
00:36:49,030 --> 00:36:49,560
Goodbye.

847
00:36:50,840 --> 00:36:51,370
Goodbye.

848
00:36:54,630 --> 00:36:55,690
Goodbye, Jianmin.

849
00:36:56,000 --> 00:36:56,530
Goodbye.

850
00:36:57,450 --> 00:37:01,300
♪ The song of life plays on ♪

851
00:37:01,580 --> 00:37:04,930
♪ Eyes no longer frail and drawn ♪

852
00:37:05,070 --> 00:37:07,870
♪ Flowers bloom in silence ♪

853
00:37:07,900 --> 00:37:11,220
♪ When we least expect them to appear ♪

854
00:37:12,990 --> 00:37:16,680
♪ Ordinary roads pave the way ♪

855
00:37:17,030 --> 00:37:20,700
♪ For extraordinary dreams to stay ♪

856
00:37:20,950 --> 00:37:32,290
♪ I will always be by your side ♪

857
00:37:43,070 --> 00:37:43,590
Zheng.

858
00:37:45,270 --> 00:37:46,270
Court Pres. Ding.

859
00:37:47,440 --> 00:37:48,500
What are you doing?

860
00:37:49,630 --> 00:37:50,280
Nothing.

861
00:37:50,960 --> 00:37:52,360
What do you mean nothing?

862
00:37:54,110 --> 00:37:55,190
Really, nothing.

863
00:37:57,400 --> 00:37:58,400
Come to my office.

864
00:37:58,800 --> 00:37:59,360
Yes.

865
00:38:10,320 --> 00:38:12,180
Eat slowly, no one's rushing you.

866
00:38:14,760 --> 00:38:15,560
What's wrong?

867
00:38:16,850 --> 00:38:18,080
I thought it was your dad.

868
00:38:18,080 --> 00:38:18,840
Look.

869
00:38:19,440 --> 00:38:21,240
I was afraid
your dad would suddenly come back.

870
00:38:21,240 --> 00:38:22,070
Why are you always

871
00:38:22,070 --> 00:38:23,030
so afraid of him?

872
00:38:23,280 --> 00:38:24,590
Do you feel guilty when you see him?

873
00:38:24,590 --> 00:38:25,470
No, no, no.

874
00:38:26,000 --> 00:38:27,000
I actually have a

875
00:38:27,890 --> 00:38:29,020
natural fear of him.

876
00:38:36,480 --> 00:38:37,360
Is it delicious?

877
00:38:37,360 --> 00:38:38,910
You know it is.

878
00:38:39,150 --> 00:38:40,210
It's so delicious.

879
00:38:40,630 --> 00:38:41,840
There's plenty more there.

880
00:38:41,840 --> 00:38:42,900
enough for the five of you

881
00:38:42,900 --> 00:38:43,900
to eat on the road.

882
00:38:49,870 --> 00:38:50,760
This is for you.

883
00:38:54,800 --> 00:38:56,440
Keep it for yourself.

884
00:38:57,110 --> 00:38:58,310
Don't let them see it.

885
00:38:59,590 --> 00:39:00,850
What's wrong with you?

886
00:39:01,920 --> 00:39:02,550
Nothing.

887
00:39:03,440 --> 00:39:04,190
Nothing?

888
00:39:05,280 --> 00:39:05,960
No.

889
00:39:09,030 --> 00:39:10,890
Ding Rui, I'll tell you the truth.

890
00:39:11,110 --> 00:39:12,440
I'm a pragmatic person.

891
00:39:13,230 --> 00:39:14,360
I don't like to brag.

892
00:39:14,880 --> 00:39:16,360
Just watch my actions.

893
00:39:17,320 --> 00:39:18,920
What actions can you take?

894
00:39:19,780 --> 00:39:20,760
You don't know how hard

895
00:39:20,760 --> 00:39:21,550
my life is.

896
00:39:23,320 --> 00:39:24,980
My mom's cooking is terrible.

897
00:39:25,760 --> 00:39:27,510
It's absolutely tragic, you know?

898
00:39:27,510 --> 00:39:27,960
So,

899
00:39:27,980 --> 00:39:29,580
from the first time I saw you,

900
00:39:29,840 --> 00:39:30,500
I swore that

901
00:39:30,800 --> 00:39:32,130
no matter what it takes,

902
00:39:32,510 --> 00:39:33,710
I will bring you home.

903
00:39:35,630 --> 00:39:36,160
Bring...

904
00:39:36,480 --> 00:39:36,960
Wait,

905
00:39:37,320 --> 00:39:38,920
who said you could bring me home?

906
00:39:38,920 --> 00:39:39,880
Did I agree?

907
00:39:40,030 --> 00:39:41,260
I can go to your house too.

908
00:39:41,260 --> 00:39:42,110
I'm just a little afraid of your dad,

909
00:39:42,110 --> 00:39:42,770
but I can go.

910
00:39:42,880 --> 00:39:43,280
No,

911
00:39:43,300 --> 00:39:44,190
you can go to my house

912
00:39:44,190 --> 00:39:45,500
and teach my mom how to cook.

913
00:39:45,500 --> 00:39:46,910
Then come back soon.

914
00:39:48,900 --> 00:39:50,830
You're making me not want to leave.

915
00:39:52,420 --> 00:39:53,550
Time to eat big buns.

916
00:39:55,360 --> 00:39:55,920
Don't

917
00:39:57,030 --> 00:39:58,480
reach for what's

918
00:39:58,510 --> 00:39:59,630
beyond your grasp.

919
00:40:00,550 --> 00:40:01,810
I didn't say anything.

920
00:40:01,850 --> 00:40:03,870
It's good that you didn't.

921
00:40:11,580 --> 00:40:13,170
[Nanyu County People's Court Further Education Application Form]

922
00:40:11,780 --> 00:40:12,910
When did you decide?

923
00:40:15,710 --> 00:40:16,320
Actually,

924
00:40:16,960 --> 00:40:19,360
I've been thinking about it
for a long time.

925
00:40:31,630 --> 00:40:33,360
Secretary Su was transferred.

926
00:40:34,590 --> 00:40:36,850
Court Pres. Zhang was also transferred.

927
00:40:36,920 --> 00:40:38,030
Our court

928
00:40:39,110 --> 00:40:41,480
needs to restructure its personnel.

929
00:40:42,150 --> 00:40:43,410
We also need to bring in

930
00:40:43,630 --> 00:40:45,160
some young backbone staff.

931
00:40:45,440 --> 00:40:47,150
I wasn't originally planning

932
00:40:48,150 --> 00:40:50,150
to keep you in administrative work,

933
00:40:53,360 --> 00:40:55,550
switching you to substantive legal work.

934
00:40:55,550 --> 00:40:57,150
Thank you, Court Pres. Ding.

935
00:40:57,670 --> 00:40:59,400
The reason I applied for further study

936
00:40:59,400 --> 00:41:00,150
was because I wanted to do

937
00:41:00,150 --> 00:41:01,090
law-related work.

938
00:41:01,090 --> 00:41:02,150
I want to be a judge.

939
00:41:04,960 --> 00:41:05,400
But,

940
00:41:08,800 --> 00:41:10,150
I want to build my foundation first,

941
00:41:10,150 --> 00:41:11,150
plan for the long term,

942
00:41:11,150 --> 00:41:12,480
then make another push.

943
00:41:14,670 --> 00:41:16,030
Working here with me,

944
00:41:16,360 --> 00:41:18,090
wouldn't let you push forward?

945
00:41:18,840 --> 00:41:20,640
That's not long‑term planning?

946
00:41:21,880 --> 00:41:22,630
Court Pres. Ding, I...

947
00:41:22,630 --> 00:41:23,800
I didn't mean that.

948
00:41:29,510 --> 00:41:31,110
Go on, then.

949
00:41:32,430 --> 00:41:33,760
Go on.

950
00:41:37,070 --> 00:41:38,440
I knew it all along.

951
00:41:41,070 --> 00:41:43,270
The moment those law students arrived,

952
00:41:43,880 --> 00:41:44,740
they were bound

953
00:41:45,510 --> 00:41:47,320
to shake up my ranks.

954
00:41:52,590 --> 00:41:54,190
Thank you, Court Pres. Ding.

955
00:41:55,230 --> 00:41:55,840
I...

956
00:41:56,510 --> 00:41:58,110
I will definitely come back.

957
00:42:13,720 --> 00:42:14,980
Director, she's here.

958
00:42:16,150 --> 00:42:16,950
Director Wei.

959
00:42:18,670 --> 00:42:20,400
Why are you so late?

960
00:42:20,590 --> 00:42:21,570
You incorrigible...

961
00:42:21,570 --> 00:42:22,320
Lei Fugen!

962
00:42:22,640 --> 00:42:23,700
What are you doing?

963
00:42:24,480 --> 00:42:25,610
If you don't behave,

964
00:42:25,670 --> 00:42:27,030
you'll be locked up again.

965
00:42:27,030 --> 00:42:28,490
How could I, Director Wei?

966
00:42:28,510 --> 00:42:30,320
I didn't commit a serious crime.

967
00:42:34,590 --> 00:42:36,450
This is the third time this month.

968
00:42:36,710 --> 00:42:37,710
If it happens again,

969
00:42:37,710 --> 00:42:39,280
he's got enough for a private cell.

970
00:42:39,280 --> 00:42:40,190
I'll definitely talk to him

971
00:42:40,190 --> 00:42:41,120
when we get back.

972
00:42:42,200 --> 00:42:42,960
Sorry.

973
00:42:44,920 --> 00:42:45,550
Don't let him

974
00:42:45,550 --> 00:42:46,810
ruin your livelihood.

975
00:42:46,960 --> 00:42:47,760
No, he won't.

976
00:42:48,000 --> 00:42:50,330
He just drinks too much and makes trouble.

977
00:42:50,360 --> 00:42:51,560
He's fine when sober.

978
00:42:52,000 --> 00:42:52,600
Lei Fugen,

979
00:42:53,150 --> 00:42:54,210
listen carefully.

980
00:42:54,970 --> 00:42:56,190
If you drink and make trouble again,

981
00:42:56,190 --> 00:42:57,720
it won't just be detention.

982
00:42:58,030 --> 00:42:59,280
Yes, Director Wei.

983
00:42:59,840 --> 00:43:01,070
Thank you, Director Wei.

984
00:43:01,070 --> 00:43:02,230
We're leaving now. Thank you.
